  "Question": "Which of these numbers is less than its reciprocal?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-2\\)",
    "B": "\\(-1\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(1\\)",
    "E": "\\(2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The reciprocal of a nonzero number \\(n\\) is \\(1/n\\). For \\(-2\\), the reciprocal is \\(-1/2\\), and\n\\[\n-2<-\\frac12.\n\\]\nThis inequality holds because \\(-2\\) lies farther left on the number line. The numbers \\(-1\\) and \\(1\\) equal their reciprocals, while \\(2>1/2\\). Zero has no reciprocal because multiplying zero by any number gives zero, never one. Thus the only qualifying number is \\(-2\\), choice A.",
